diff --git a/lib/emulator_core/control_port.ml b/lib/emulator_core/control_port.ml
deleted file mode 100644
index 24370bf..0000000
--- a/lib/emulator_core/control_port.ml
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,171 +0,0 @@
-(* University of Florida *)
-(* Author: Bohdan Purtell *)
-(* Module: "control_port.ml" *)
-(* The core control port: the request, decision, and status records shared by every
-   producer of core control.
-
-   [Emulator_core] owns this contract. [Host_link] (over serial) and
-   [Simulator_backend] (directly in Cyclesim) are two transports over it. The records are
-   direction-neutral; a module embeds them with its own [_i] or [_o] suffix, so the fields
-   keep the port names they had before the records existed. This module depends only on
-   the width definitions of [Program_memory_controller], [Execution_unit], and [Protemu_isa], never
-   on a consumer.
-
-   Step, pin claim/release, queues, pads, and program RAM are not part of this port. They
-   remain separate ports of [Emulator_core], and a transport that does not use them ties
-   them off.
-
-   Temporal contract. Every statement is derived from [Emulator_core], [Program_memory_controller],
-   and both producers as they exist, not from a cleaner handshake.
-
-   1. Offers. Each rising edge of the core clock with a [*_valid] field high is one offer
-      of that request, decided in that cycle. There is no ready signal, stall, or held
-      offer: the core never defers a decision to a later cycle. A valid that stays high is
-      a new offer on the next edge, decided against the updated state. Both producers
-      raise a valid for exactly one cycle per operation and never re-offer automatically.
-
-   2. Operands. An operand is meaningful only in a cycle where its request's valid is
-      high. It must be stable before the sampling edge of that cycle. The core consumes it
-      then and registers what a later cycle needs (image length, verify flag, expected
-      word), so operands need not stay stable after the offer. [Host_link] drives
-      them continuously from its retained request registers; [Simulator_backend] drives
-      them only in the offer cycle and zeroes them otherwise.
-
-   3. Decisions. Acceptance is combinational from the offer and the current core state. It
-      is observed in the offer cycle, before the sampling edge. Its effect is visible
-      after that edge. Rejection is [valid & ~accepted]: during a valid offer exactly one
-      of the pair is high, and with no offer both are low. Both signals are kept even
-      though [Host_link] reads only acceptance.
-
-   4. Arbitration. Neither producer offers two requests in one cycle, but the core
-      resolves simultaneous offers as follows.
-      - ABORT is accepted whenever offered while enabled and out of reset. It halts
-        execution at that edge, which refuses every other request in the same cycle.
-      - STOP is accepted whenever offered while enabled, out of reset, and without an
-        ABORT offer, whatever the execution state. It refuses a simultaneous RUN. It does
-        not itself refuse program requests; only a pause that it causes at an instruction
-        boundary in that cycle does.
-      - Program requests need the core halted, engines idle, and no execution halt in that
-        cycle. Among themselves the order is LOAD_START, LOAD_WRITE, READBACK,
-        LOAD_COMPLETE, by validity rather than acceptance: a higher offer refuses the
-        lower ones even if it is itself refused.
-      - RUN is refused by any program request, STOP or ABORT offer, or step request in the
-        same cycle.
-
-   5. READBACK completion. Acceptance issues the RAM read at the sampling edge. The
-      response fields are registered: for an offer accepted at edge E,
-      [readback_response_valid] is high for exactly the cycle between edges E+1 and E+2,
-      and [readback_response_data] and [readback_response_match] are meaningful only then.
-      A second READBACK is refused while the response is outstanding. Reset, disable, an
-      accepted ABORT, or an accepted LOAD_START in the cycle between E and E+1 cancels the
-      response; it never appears later. [Host_link] waits for the valid pulse with
-      no bound. [Simulator_backend] requires it in the next post-edge observation and
-      reports its absence as a backend invariant.
-
-   6. ABORT completion. Acceptance is not cleanup. Cleanup is complete when the status
-      shows [halted], [engines_idle], and zero [pin_oe], [software_claim], and
-      [engine_claim]. The core completes cleanup at the accepting edge (P3.3's control
-      contract; P3.4's prompt completion boundary), so the first observation after that
-      edge shows it. [Host_link] waits for that condition with no bound before
-      responding. [Simulator_backend] does not wait: it reports completion only if that
-      single observation shows it.
-
-   7. STOP completion. Acceptance is not halting. If execution is active, the core latches
-      the request and halts at the next instruction boundary; there is no bound on how
-      long that takes. Halting is observed only through [Status.halted]. A STOP accepted
-      while already halted leaves nothing pending, so a later RUN is not paused by it.
-
-   8. Reset and disable. While [reset_i] is high or [en_i] is low, every offer is refused:
-      its accepted signal is low and its rejected signal follows its valid. Either one
-      cancels an outstanding READBACK response and any pending STOP. Disable halts
-      execution and cancels mechanisms but preserves a completed image; reset also
-      invalidates it. [Host_link] also discards its own dispatch, wait, and response
-      state; [Simulator_backend] holds no request across cycles.
-
-   9. Status. Every [Status] field is a live observation of core state, not an event, and
-      has no valid qualifier. [Host_link] samples it before an edge: in a command's
-      dispatch cycle to classify a refusal or build a STATUS response, and on each cycle
-      of an ABORT wait. [Simulator_backend] samples it after an edge, and classifies a
-      refusal from the status observed before it drives the offer.
-*)
-
-open! Core
-open! Hardcaml
-open! Signal
-
-(* The shared request subset. A field is a valid bit or an operand of the request named by
-   its prefix. Addresses and lengths keep [Program_memory_controller]'s request width, one bit wider
-   than the physical port, so the core checks bounds before narrowing.
-*)
-module Request = struct
-  type 'a t =
-    { load_start_valid : 'a
-    ; load_length : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.request_address_bits]
-    ; load_write_valid : 'a
-    ; load_address : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.request_address_bits]
-    ; load_data : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.program_width]
-    ; load_complete_valid : 'a
-    ; readback_valid : 'a
-    ; readback_address : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.request_address_bits]
-    ; readback_verify : 'a
-    ; readback_expected : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.program_width]
-    ; run_valid : 'a
-    ; stop_valid : 'a
-    ; abort_valid : 'a
-    }
-  [@@deriving hardcaml]
-end
-
-(* Per-request decisions in [Request]'s order, plus the registered READBACK response. See
-   items 3 and 5 of the contract above.
-*)
-module Decision = struct
-  type 'a t =
-    { load_start_accepted : 'a
-    ; load_start_rejected : 'a
-    ; load_write_accepted : 'a
-    ; load_write_rejected : 'a
-    ; load_complete_accepted : 'a
-    ; load_complete_rejected : 'a
-    ; readback_accepted : 'a
-    ; readback_rejected : 'a
-    ; readback_response_valid : 'a
-    ; readback_response_data : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.program_width]
-    ; readback_response_match : 'a
-    ; run_accepted : 'a
-    ; run_rejected : 'a
-    ; stop_accepted : 'a
-    ; stop_rejected : 'a
-    ; abort_accepted : 'a
-    ; abort_rejected : 'a
-    }
-  [@@deriving hardcaml]
-end
-
-(* Core observations that a transport reports or uses to classify a refusal; see item 9.
-   [pin_oe], [software_claim], and [engine_claim] are observations only, used for STATUS
-   flags and ABORT cleanup. Pin claim and release are not requests on this port.
-*)
-module Status = struct
-  type 'a t =
-    { halted : 'a
-    ; engines_idle : 'a
-    ; image_valid : 'a
-    ; load_active : 'a
-    ; image_length : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.request_address_bits]
-    ; words_written : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.request_address_bits]
-    ; words_verified : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.request_address_bits]
-    ; verification_failed : 'a
-    ; fetch_fault : 'a
-    ; execution_active : 'a
-    ; normal_halt : 'a
-    ; execution_fault : 'a
-    ; fault_kind : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Fault.width]
-    ; pc : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.pc_bits]
-    ; phase : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Phase.width]
-    ; pin_oe : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; software_claim : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; engine_claim : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    }
-  [@@deriving hardcaml]
-end
diff --git a/lib/emulator_core/emulator_core.ml b/lib/emulator_core/emulator_core.ml
deleted file mode 100644
index 5824918..0000000
--- a/lib/emulator_core/emulator_core.ml
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,413 +0,0 @@
-(* University of Florida *)
-(* Author: Bohdan Purtell *)
-(* Module: "emulator_core.ml" *)
-(* P3.3 production composition of program access, execution, and P2 mechanisms.
-
-   Program RAM remains an external latency-one port. STOP pauses only at P3.2's existing
-   instruction boundary, ABORT cancels immediately, and a step resumes preserved state for
-   one instruction. Program access receives the adapter's real engine-idle indication.
-
-   Host control crosses [Control_port], which this module owns: requests arrive as
-   [control_request_i], decisions leave as [control_decision_o], and [control_status]
-   gathers the status observations. Step, pin claims, queues, and pads remain separate
-   ports.
-*)
-
-open! Core
-open! Hardcaml
-open! Signal
-
-module I = struct
-  type 'a t =
-    { clock_i : 'a
-    ; reset_i : 'a
-    ; en_i : 'a
-    ; (* Shared control requests; see [Control_port] for the temporal contract. Each field
-         keeps its flat port name, such as [load_start_valid_i]. *)
-      control_request_i : 'a Control_port.Request.t [@rtlsuffix "_i"]
-    ; step_valid_i : 'a
-    ; prog_mem_read_data_i : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.program_width]
-    ; pin_async_i : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; occupied_i : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; software_claim_valid_i : 'a
-    ; software_claim_mask_i : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; software_release_valid_i : 'a
-    ; software_release_mask_i : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; tx_ready_i : 'a
-    ; rx_valid_i : 'a
-    ; rx_data_i : 'a [@bits 8]
-    ; transfer_rx_ready_i : 'a
-    }
-  [@@deriving hardcaml ~rtlmangle:false]
-end
-
-module O = struct
-  type 'a t =
-    { prog_mem_enable_o : 'a
-    ; prog_mem_write_enable_o : 'a
-    ; prog_mem_address_o : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.program_address_bits]
-    ; prog_mem_write_data_o : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.program_width]
-    ; (* Shared control decisions; see [Control_port]. Flat names, such as
-         [load_start_accepted_o]. [control_status] gathers the shared status below. *)
-      control_decision_o : 'a Control_port.Decision.t [@rtlsuffix "_o"]
-    ; step_accepted_o : 'a
-    ; step_rejected_o : 'a
-    ; halted_o : 'a
-    ; engines_idle_o : 'a
-    ; image_valid_o : 'a
-    ; load_active_o : 'a
-    ; image_length_o : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.request_address_bits]
-    ; words_written_o : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.request_address_bits]
-    ; words_verified_o : 'a [@bits Program_memory_controller.Config.request_address_bits]
-    ; verification_failed_o : 'a
-    ; fetch_fault_o : 'a
-    ; execution_active_o : 'a
-    ; normal_halt_o : 'a
-    ; execution_fault_o : 'a
-    ; fault_kind_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Fault.width]
-    ; fault_instruction_slot_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.pc_bits]
-    ; fault_address_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.pc_bits]
-    ; fault_reason_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.mechanism_reason_bits]
-    ; instruction_boundary_o : 'a
-    ; retired_o : 'a
-    ; pc_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.pc_bits]
-    ; registers_o : 'a [@bits 128]
-    ; zero_o : 'a
-    ; carry_o : 'a
-    ; negative_o : 'a
-    ; descriptor_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.descriptor_bits]
-    ; phase_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Phase.width]
-    ; fetch_cycles_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.count_bits]
-    ; execute_cycles_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.count_bits]
-    ; stall_cycles_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.count_bits]
-    ; instruction_count_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.count_bits]
-    ; extension_fetches_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.count_bits]
-    ; total_cycles_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.count_bits]
-    ; mechanism_request_valid_o : 'a
-    ; mechanism_kind_o : 'a [@bits Execution_unit.Config.mechanism_kind_bits]
-    ; mechanism_accepted_o : 'a
-    ; mechanism_refused_o : 'a
-    ; mechanism_completion_valid_o : 'a
-    ; snapshot_o : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; rising_o : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; falling_o : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; status_o : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Event_kind.count]
-    ; status_overflow_o : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Event_kind.count]
-    ; pins_o : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; pin_oe_o : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; software_claim_o : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; engine_claim_o : 'a [@bits Protemu_isa.Pins.count]
-    ; software_request_rejected_o : 'a
-    ; bank_conflict_o : 'a
-    ; timing_busy_o : 'a
-    ; transfer_busy_o : 'a
-    ; transfer_done_o : 'a
-    ; transfer_fault_o : 'a
-    ; transfer_rx_valid_o : 'a
-    ; transfer_rx_data_o : 'a [@bits 32]
-    ; tx_valid_o : 'a
-    ; tx_data_o : 'a [@bits 8]
-    ; rx_ready_o : 'a
-    ; tx_count_o : 'a [@bits 5]
-    ; rx_count_o : 'a [@bits 5]
-    }
-  [@@deriving hardcaml ~rtlmangle:false]
-end
-
-(* The shared [Control_port.Status] observations, gathered from their [O] ports. They stay
-   flat ports rather than one embedded record because they are not contiguous in [O], and
-   embedding them would reorder the emitted module's ports.
-*)
-let control_status (o : 'a O.t) : 'a Control_port.Status.t =
-  { halted = o.halted_o
-  ; engines_idle = o.engines_idle_o
-  ; image_valid = o.image_valid_o
-  ; load_active = o.load_active_o
-  ; image_length = o.image_length_o
-  ; words_written = o.words_written_o
-  ; words_verified = o.words_verified_o
-  ; verification_failed = o.verification_failed_o
-  ; fetch_fault = o.fetch_fault_o
-  ; execution_active = o.execution_active_o
-  ; normal_halt = o.normal_halt_o
-  ; execution_fault = o.execution_fault_o
-  ; fault_kind = o.fault_kind_o
-  ; pc = o.pc_o
-  ; phase = o.phase_o
-  ; pin_oe = o.pin_oe_o
-  ; software_claim = o.software_claim_o
-  ; engine_claim = o.engine_claim_o
-  }
-;;
-
-[@@@ocamlformat "disable"]
-
-module I_Regs = struct
-  type 'a t =
-    { stop_pending : 'a
-    ; stepping     : 'a
-    }
-  [@@deriving hardcaml]
-end
-
-let create (scope : Scope.t) (i : _ I.t) : _ O.t =
-  let open Always in
-  let spec = Reg_spec.create ~clock:i.clock_i ~clear:i.reset_i () in
-  let request = i.control_request_i in
-  let r = I_Regs.Of_always.reg spec in
-  I_Regs.Of_always.apply_names ~prefix:"reg_" ~naming_op:(Scope.naming scope) r;
-
-  let fetch_valid = wire 1 in
-  let fetch_address = wire Program_memory_controller.Config.request_address_bits in
-  let core_execution_halt = wire 1 in
-  let execution_halt = wire 1 in
-  let engine_idle = wire 1 in
-  let execution_boundary = wire 1 in
-  let execution_active = wire 1 in
-  let execution_fault = wire 1 in
-  let normal_halt = wire 1 in
-  let mechanism_request = wire 1 in
-  let mechanism_kind = wire Execution_unit.Config.mechanism_kind_bits in
-  let mechanism_arg0 = wire 16 in
-  let mechanism_arg1 = wire 16 in
-  let mechanism_arg2 = wire 16 in
-  let mechanism_timeout = wire 1 in
-  let mechanism_descriptor = wire Execution_unit.Config.descriptor_bits in
-  let mechanism_accepted = wire 1 in
-  let mechanism_refused = wire 1 in
-  let mechanism_refusal_reason = wire Execution_unit.Config.mechanism_reason_bits in
-  let mechanism_completion = wire 1 in
-  let mechanism_result = wire 16 in
-  let mechanism_completion_fault = wire 1 in
-  let mechanism_completion_reason = wire Execution_unit.Config.mechanism_reason_bits in
-
-  let abort_offer = request.abort_valid &: i.en_i &: ~:(i.reset_i) in
-  let stop_offer = request.stop_valid &: i.en_i &: ~:(i.reset_i) &: ~:abort_offer in
-  let step_offer =
-    i.step_valid_i
-    &: i.en_i
-    &: ~:(i.reset_i)
-    &: ~:abort_offer
-    &: ~:stop_offer
-  in
-  let run_offer =
-    request.run_valid
-    &: ~:abort_offer
-    &: ~:stop_offer
-    &: ~:(i.step_valid_i)
-  in
-  let access_run = wire 1 in
-  let access =
-    Program_memory_controller.create
-      (Scope.sub_scope scope "access")
-      { Program_memory_controller.I.clock_i = i.clock_i
-      ; reset_i = i.reset_i
-      ; en_i = i.en_i
-      ; engines_idle_i = engine_idle
-      ; load_start_valid_i = request.load_start_valid
-      ; load_length_i = request.load_length
-      ; load_write_valid_i = request.load_write_valid
-      ; load_address_i = request.load_address
-      ; load_data_i = request.load_data
-      ; load_complete_valid_i = request.load_complete_valid
-      ; readback_valid_i = request.readback_valid
-      ; readback_address_i = request.readback_address
-      ; readback_verify_i = request.readback_verify
-      ; readback_expected_i = request.readback_expected
-      ; run_valid_i = access_run
-      ; execution_halt_i = execution_halt
-      ; fetch_valid_i = fetch_valid
-      ; fetch_address_i = fetch_address
-      ; prog_mem_read_data_i = i.prog_mem_read_data_i
-      }
-  in
-  let step_candidate =
-    step_offer
-    &: access.halted_o
-    &: engine_idle
-    &: ~:execution_fault
-    &: ~:normal_halt
-  in
-  assign access_run (run_offer |: step_candidate);
-  let run_accepted = access.run_accepted_o &: run_offer in
-  let step_accepted = access.run_accepted_o &: step_candidate in
-  let stop_accepted = stop_offer in
-  let abort_accepted = abort_offer in
-
-  let pause_for_stop = (r.stop_pending.value |: stop_accepted) &: execution_boundary in
-  let pause_for_step = r.stepping.value &: execution_boundary in
-  let pause = pause_for_stop |: pause_for_step in
-  assign execution_halt (core_execution_halt |: abort_accepted |: pause);
-
-  let execution =
-    Execution_unit.create
-      (Scope.sub_scope scope "execution")
-      { Execution_unit.I.clock_i = i.clock_i
-      ; reset_i = i.reset_i
-      ; en_i = i.en_i
-      ; run_accepted_i = run_accepted
-      ; resume_i = step_accepted
-      ; pause_i = pause
-      ; abort_i = abort_accepted
-      ; fetch_accepted_i = access.fetch_accepted_o
-      ; fetch_rejected_i = access.fetch_rejected_o
-      ; fetch_fault_i = access.fetch_fault_event_o
-      ; fetch_completion_valid_i = access.fetch_completion_valid_o
-      ; fetch_completion_data_i = access.fetch_completion_data_o
-      ; mechanism_accepted_i = mechanism_accepted
-      ; mechanism_refused_i = mechanism_refused
-      ; mechanism_refusal_reason_i = mechanism_refusal_reason
-      ; mechanism_completion_valid_i = mechanism_completion
-      ; mechanism_completion_result_i = mechanism_result
-      ; mechanism_completion_fault_i = mechanism_completion_fault
-      ; mechanism_completion_reason_i = mechanism_completion_reason
-      }
-  in
-  assign fetch_valid execution.fetch_valid_o;
-  assign fetch_address execution.fetch_address_o;
-  assign core_execution_halt execution.execution_halt_o;
-  assign execution_boundary execution.instruction_boundary_o;
-  assign execution_active execution.active_o;
-  assign execution_fault execution.execution_fault_o;
-  assign normal_halt execution.normal_halt_o;
-  assign mechanism_request execution.mechanism_request_valid_o;
-  assign mechanism_kind execution.mechanism_kind_o;
-  assign mechanism_arg0 execution.mechanism_arg0_o;
-  assign mechanism_arg1 execution.mechanism_arg1_o;
-  assign mechanism_arg2 execution.mechanism_arg2_o;
-  assign mechanism_timeout execution.mechanism_timeout_enable_o;
-  assign mechanism_descriptor execution.mechanism_descriptor_o;
-
-  let mechanisms =
-    Primitive_dispatch.create
-      (Scope.sub_scope scope "mechanisms")
-      { Primitive_dispatch.I.clock_i = i.clock_i
-      ; reset_i = i.reset_i
-      ; en_i = i.en_i
-      ; abort_i = abort_accepted
-      ; abort_event_i = abort_accepted &: (execution_active |: ~:engine_idle)
-      ; pin_async_i = i.pin_async_i
-      ; occupied_i = i.occupied_i
-      ; mechanism_request_valid_i = mechanism_request
-      ; mechanism_kind_i = mechanism_kind
-      ; mechanism_arg0_i = mechanism_arg0
-      ; mechanism_arg1_i = mechanism_arg1
-      ; mechanism_arg2_i = mechanism_arg2
-      ; mechanism_timeout_enable_i = mechanism_timeout
-      ; mechanism_descriptor_i = mechanism_descriptor
-      ; software_claim_valid_i = i.software_claim_valid_i
-      ; software_claim_mask_i = i.software_claim_mask_i
-      ; software_release_valid_i = i.software_release_valid_i
-      ; software_release_mask_i = i.software_release_mask_i
-      ; tx_ready_i = i.tx_ready_i
-      ; rx_valid_i = i.rx_valid_i
-      ; rx_data_i = i.rx_data_i
-      ; transfer_rx_ready_i = i.transfer_rx_ready_i
-      }
-  in
-  assign engine_idle mechanisms.engines_idle_o;
-  assign mechanism_accepted mechanisms.mechanism_accepted_o;
-  assign mechanism_refused mechanisms.mechanism_refused_o;
-  assign mechanism_refusal_reason mechanisms.mechanism_refusal_reason_o;
-  assign mechanism_completion mechanisms.mechanism_completion_valid_o;
-  assign mechanism_result mechanisms.mechanism_completion_result_o;
-  assign mechanism_completion_fault mechanisms.mechanism_completion_fault_o;
-  assign mechanism_completion_reason mechanisms.mechanism_completion_reason_o;
-
-  compile
-    [ r.stop_pending <-- r.stop_pending.value
-    ; r.stepping <-- r.stepping.value
-    ; when_ (stop_accepted &: ~:(access.halted_o)) [ r.stop_pending <--. 1 ]
-    ; when_ step_accepted [ r.stepping <--. 1 ]
-    ; when_ pause_for_stop [ r.stop_pending <--. 0 ]
-    ; when_ pause_for_step [ r.stepping <--. 0 ]
-    ; when_ (run_accepted |: abort_accepted |: ~:(i.en_i))
-        [ r.stop_pending <--. 0; r.stepping <--. 0 ]
-    ];
-
-  { O.prog_mem_enable_o = access.prog_mem_enable_o
-  ; prog_mem_write_enable_o = access.prog_mem_write_enable_o
-  ; prog_mem_address_o = access.prog_mem_address_o
-  ; prog_mem_write_data_o = access.prog_mem_write_data_o
-  ; control_decision_o =
-      { Control_port.Decision.load_start_accepted = access.load_start_accepted_o
-      ; load_start_rejected     = access.load_start_rejected_o
-      ; load_write_accepted     = access.load_write_accepted_o
-      ; load_write_rejected     = access.load_write_rejected_o
-      ; load_complete_accepted  = access.load_complete_accepted_o
-      ; load_complete_rejected  = access.load_complete_rejected_o
-      ; readback_accepted       = access.readback_accepted_o
-      ; readback_rejected       = access.readback_rejected_o
-      ; readback_response_valid = access.readback_response_valid_o
-      ; readback_response_data  = access.readback_response_data_o
-      ; readback_response_match = access.readback_response_match_o
-      ; run_accepted            = run_accepted
-      ; run_rejected            = request.run_valid &: ~:run_accepted
-      ; stop_accepted           = stop_accepted
-      ; stop_rejected           = request.stop_valid &: ~:stop_accepted
-      ; abort_accepted          = abort_accepted
-      ; abort_rejected          = request.abort_valid &: ~:abort_accepted
-      }
-  ; step_accepted_o = step_accepted
-  ; step_rejected_o = i.step_valid_i &: ~:step_accepted
-  ; halted_o = access.halted_o
-  ; engines_idle_o = engine_idle
-  ; image_valid_o = access.image_valid_o
-  ; load_active_o = access.load_active_o
-  ; image_length_o = access.image_length_o
-  ; words_written_o = access.words_written_o
-  ; words_verified_o = access.words_verified_o
-  ; verification_failed_o = access.verification_failed_o
-  ; fetch_fault_o = access.fetch_fault_o
-  ; execution_active_o = execution.active_o
-  ; normal_halt_o = execution.normal_halt_o
-  ; execution_fault_o = execution.execution_fault_o
-  ; fault_kind_o = execution.fault_kind_o
-  ; fault_instruction_slot_o = execution.fault_instruction_slot_o
-  ; fault_address_o = execution.fault_address_o
-  ; fault_reason_o = execution.fault_reason_o
-  ; instruction_boundary_o = execution.instruction_boundary_o
-  ; retired_o = execution.retired_o
-  ; pc_o = execution.pc_o
-  ; registers_o = execution.registers_o
-  ; zero_o = execution.zero_o
-  ; carry_o = execution.carry_o
-  ; negative_o = execution.negative_o
-  ; descriptor_o = execution.descriptor_o
-  ; phase_o = execution.phase_o
-  ; fetch_cycles_o = execution.fetch_cycles_o
-  ; execute_cycles_o = execution.execute_cycles_o
-  ; stall_cycles_o = execution.stall_cycles_o
-  ; instruction_count_o = execution.instruction_count_o
-  ; extension_fetches_o = execution.extension_fetches_o
-  ; total_cycles_o = execution.total_cycles_o
-  ; mechanism_request_valid_o = mechanism_request
-  ; mechanism_kind_o = mechanism_kind
-  ; mechanism_accepted_o = mechanism_accepted
-  ; mechanism_refused_o = mechanism_refused
-  ; mechanism_completion_valid_o = mechanism_completion
-  ; snapshot_o = mechanisms.snapshot_o
-  ; rising_o = mechanisms.rising_o
-  ; falling_o = mechanisms.falling_o
-  ; status_o = mechanisms.status_o
-  ; status_overflow_o = mechanisms.status_overflow_o
-  ; pins_o = mechanisms.pins_o
-  ; pin_oe_o = mechanisms.pin_oe_o
-  ; software_claim_o = mechanisms.software_claim_o
-  ; engine_claim_o = mechanisms.engine_claim_o
-  ; software_request_rejected_o = mechanisms.software_request_rejected_o
-  ; bank_conflict_o = mechanisms.bank_conflict_o
-  ; timing_busy_o = mechanisms.timing_busy_o
-  ; transfer_busy_o = mechanisms.transfer_busy_o
-  ; transfer_done_o = mechanisms.transfer_done_o
-  ; transfer_fault_o = mechanisms.transfer_fault_o
-  ; transfer_rx_valid_o = mechanisms.transfer_rx_valid_o
-  ; transfer_rx_data_o = mechanisms.transfer_rx_data_o
